  "answer": "n = 1",
  "mistakes": [],
  "hints": [
    "You need n⁵ − n to be even while n itself is odd.",
    "Try a small odd number."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Take $n = 1$: $n^5 - n = 0$, which is even, but $n = 1$ is odd.",
    "(In fact $n^5 - n$ is even for every integer, so any odd $n$ works.)"
